[length:05:11]
[ti:Crooked girl]
[ar:Aracne]
[al:Chaotic-disfuntyonal]
[au:Aracne]
[lr:Aracne]
[by:Aracne]
[re:LRC Workbench by Azaria (lrc-workbench.azariadev.dev)]
[ve:0.3.2]
[00:02.92]The radio finds me...
[00:07.10]like it knows my name...
[00:20.41]The wallpaper breathes
[00:22.09]through the radio grain
[00:23.10]like it spells my name
[00:24.16]again and again
[00:25.26]The limbo lobby gets longer
[00:26.44]when I try to explain
[00:27.77]red curtains are waiting
[00:28.99]in the back of my brain
[00:30.29]The pain has no edges
[00:31.56]just fog in my hands
[00:32.77]I keep reading old maps
[00:33.91]to a place that never stands
[00:35.36]Red curtains in my sleep
[00:36.61]rust flowers on the wall
[00:37.82]someone laughs behind the glass
[00:39.19]but there’s no one there at all
[00:40.62]They feed me Garmonbozia
[00:42.76]and call it getting wise
[00:45.36]I swallow what life gives me
[00:47.81]with panic behind my eyes
[00:50.62]The mirror keeps asking
[00:52.67]which version survived
[00:55.32]the girl who dreamed in fairies
[00:57.67]or the woman hanged alive
[01:00.34]I mistook the fall
[01:02.74]for the beginning of a life
[01:05.31]starshine on my tongue
[01:07.91]Garmonbozia in my mind
[01:10.43]But the world blurred at the edges
[01:11.93]like a dream inside a dream
[01:13.37]and every dream has endings
[01:15.59]even when it lets you scream
[01:20.58]I jumped from the cliff as The Fool
[01:22.21]with the stars shining on my side
[01:25.63]but I woke as the Crooked Girl
[01:27.38]with the world upside down
[01:30.56]The edge became a rope
[01:31.94]and stranded me in the air
[01:35.48]hands tied behind my back
[01:37.26]watching rust bloom everywhere
[01:40.69]I didn’t fall down
[01:42.49]I got caught halfway
[01:43.76]on a black-and-white floor
[01:44.93]between starlight and pain
[01:46.19]Crooked Girl
[01:47.43]with crooked visions
[01:48.79]I lost the ground
[01:50.06]and I don’t know who I am now
[01:52.38]Crooked, crooked
[01:53.21]girl, girl
[01:54.18]caught half
[01:54.86]halfway
[01:56.47]Crooked, crooked
[01:57.98]girl, girl
[01:58.92]rust blooms
[02:00.01]everywhere
[02:01.45]The red room kept breathing
[02:02.98]like it knew I wasn’t there
[02:04.15]red curtains softly moving
[02:05.36]sreyarp elttil nettor revo
[02:06.51]I used to call it future
[02:07.83]when the dark began to shine
[02:08.90]now every open doorway
[02:10.17]looks like a labyrinth in disguise
[02:12.16]The girl in the starlight
[02:13.46]saw a kingdom in the dust
[02:15.05]but the woman upside down
[02:16.02]only sees how everything rusts
[02:17.95]And I can’t stop the fog
[02:19.16]I can’t turn the story back
[02:20.37]I can only hear the metal
[02:21.61]grow white flowers through the cracks
[02:24.13]The mirror keeps asking
[02:26.49]which version was real
[02:29.05]the one who kept becoming
[02:31.25]or the one who learned to kneel
[02:33.72]I mistook the falling
[02:36.34]for a door into my life
[02:38.93]but the door became a ceiling
[02:41.45]and the ceiling held the rope
[02:44.41]I jumped as The Fool
[02:46.56]with stars in my mouth
[02:49.02]but I woke as the Crooked Girl
[02:51.06]with the world upside down
[02:54.03]The edge became a tether
[02:55.43]and tied me to the air
[02:59.09]hands behind my back
[03:00.77]watching rust bloom everywhere
[03:04.18]I didn’t fall down
[03:05.74]I got caught halfway
[03:07.15]on a black-and-white floor
[03:08.88]between starlight and pain
[03:09.87]Crooked Girl
[03:10.95]in a crooked mood
[03:12.24]life betrayed me
[03:13.43]and the fog came down
[03:25.52]Croo-croo- crooked-
[03:26.41]half- half- halfway-
[03:28.87]floor- floor- gone-
[03:31.40]star-star-stain-
[03:35.12]If guilt is a city
[03:36.15]then I know every street
[03:37.34]if hope is a star
[03:38.46]why is it rotting in my teeth?
[03:41.27]There’s a room behind the room
[03:42.37]where my old voice sings
[03:44.37]red curtains, dead flowers
[03:46.85]and a telephone that rings backwards
[03:49.44]I eat what they give me
[03:51.14]I laugh when it hurts
[03:52.57]I turn into anyone
[03:54.26]while the whole world rusts
[03:57.54]I was bright once
[03:59.19]wasn’t I?
[03:59.96]I was bright once
[04:01.28]wasn’t I?
[04:07.57]I jumped as The Fool
[04:09.57]with stars in my mouth
[04:12.23]but I woke as the Crooked Girl
[04:14.34]with the world upside down
[04:17.32]The cliff became a rope
[04:18.79]the sky became a ceiling
[04:19.86]I didn’t fall
[04:21.05]I was caught in the meaning
[04:22.63]I didn’t fall down
[04:24.00]I got caught halfway
[04:25.31]between a girl made out of starlight
[04:26.69]and a woman made of pain
[04:28.71]Crooked Girl
[04:30.38]in a crooked morning
[04:33.03]I lost the floor
[04:35.09]now I don’t know who I am now
[04:39.18]Crooked Girl
[04:40.61]with her hands tied back
[04:41.93]watching every golden thing
[04:44.98]turn rust, turn rust, turn black
[04:49.87]The radio blooms with static
[04:54.14]like it knows my name
[04:58.48]I used to see a kingdom
[05:01.72]now I only see the stain
